On Fri, Feb 15, 2008 at 1:29 PM, Dong Fu <dongf...@gmail.com> wrote:
>
>  Thanks Elizabeth.
>
>  What we are trying to do is to compare the results from RmaPlm() in
>  aroma.affymetrix with the results from the Rma() in affy.  We did the
>  log2 transformation of the RmaPlm() as well, but the transformed
>  result is still not comparable to the default log2 result from Rma(),
>  with about 96% correlation.
>
>  We were wondering if the RmaPlm() is implemented differently, which
>  means the results are really not comparable.

Do you mean you compare chip effect estimates from (1)
QuantileNormalization + RmaPlm with estimates from (2) rma() set to do
quantile normaliation only?

What does your (theta1, theta2) for the two estimates look like on the
intensity and the log scale?

I also forgot to specify in my previous reply that RmaPlm fit the
log-additive model on PM-only, by default.

/Henrik

>
>  Thanks.
>
>  Dong
>
>
>
>
>
>  On Feb 15, 3:16 pm, Elizabeth Purdom <epur...@gmail.com> wrote:
>  > Hi Dong,
>  > I don't know if this answers your question (Henrik can respond to the
>  > implementation question), but all results in aroma.affymetrix that are
>  > saved to .cel files are saved as 2^x (the 'intensity scale') regardless
>  > whether this is a logical scale for the values. This is true even when
>  > (as with Rma) the original calculations are done in the log2 scale --
>  > the answers are converted to 2^ for storage to be consistent with this
>  > rule. So the residuals, chip-effects, weights, probe-affinities, etc.
>  > all need to be logged if you want them back on the standard scale in
>  > which they were calculated.
>  > Best,
>  > Elizabeth
>  >
>  > Dong Fu wrote:
>  > > Hello Henrik,
>  >
>  > > What is the difference between your RmaPlm() function in
>  > > aroma.affymetrix vs. rma() in affy package?
>  >
>  > > We noticed that the results from the RmaPlm() function is not in log2
>  > > scale.  Is there a implementation difference?
>  >
>  > > Thanks.
>  >
>  > > Dong
>  >
