There is also a method writeRegions() that you can use in a very
similar way but provides more output (and correct URLs):

pathname <- writeRegions(glad, arrays=1, chromosomes=1:4,
                                 organism="Human", hgVersion="hg18");
print(pathname)
[1] "gladData/Jeremy_2007-10k,ACC,-XY,RMA,+300,A+B,FLN,-XY/Mapping10K_Xba142/Jer
emy_2007-10k,ACC,-XY,RMA,+300,A+B,FLN,-XY,regions.xls"

